From: NeoDarwin
Subject: [PATCH] libtop: the arm64 shared region

in_shared_region() knows the shared region of 32-bit ARM, Intel and
PowerPC tasks and aborts on any other CPU type ("unknown CPU type:
0x100000c"); the published source has no CPU_TYPE_ARM64 case. On an arm64
machine every task is CPU_TYPE_ARM64, so top aborts on its first sample.
Add the case, with <mach/shared_region.h>'s ARM64 base and size.

--- a/libtop.c	2026-10-05 15:17:01
+++ b/libtop.c	2026-10-05 15:17:01
@@ -770,6 +770,10 @@
 		size = SHARED_REGION_SIZE_ARM;
 		break;
 
+	case CPU_TYPE_ARM64:
+		base = SHARED_REGION_BASE_ARM64;
+		size = SHARED_REGION_SIZE_ARM64;
+		break;
 
 	case CPU_TYPE_X86_64:
 		base = SHARED_REGION_BASE_X86_64;
